n.json"} {"question" "q-68072" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No horizontal asymptote"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/state.json" "file_sha256" "794a5b783a2e6ed149688ecb4d1509c96dad9ea40a695092ba12b68371dbf4c9" "basis" 655 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ where $f(x)=\\frac{11{x}^{5}-9{x}^{6}}{2{x}^{5}-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/state.json" "file_sha256" "794a5b783a2e6ed149688ecb4d1509c96dad9ea40a695092ba12b68371dbf4c9" "basis" 655 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{5}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{11{x}^{5}-9{x}^{6}}{2{x}^{5}-1} \\\\  & {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{11{x}^{5}}{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{9{x}^{6}}{{x}^{5}})}{(\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(11-9x)}{(2-\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{11-9x}{2-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(11-9x) \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/state.json" "file_sha256" "794a5b783a2e6ed149688ecb4d1509c96dad9ea40a695092ba12b68371dbf4c9" "basis" 655 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a8fc4a62db3ddd630a473cdc2c920f268b90c9706f019f17762a4e08b4154258" "basis" 655 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106702" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/state.json" "file_sha256" "794a5b783a2e6ed149688ecb4d1509c96dad9ea40a695092ba12b68371dbf4c9" "basis" 655 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106702" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/state.json" "file_sha256" "794a5b783a2e6ed149688ecb4d1509c96dad9ea40a695092ba12b68371dbf4c9" "basis" 655 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106702" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-\\frac{11}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964951/state.json" "file_sha256" "794a5b783a2e6ed149688ecb4d1509c96dad9ea40a695092ba12b68371dbf4c9" "basis" 655 "verification" "/home/