ear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-3762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "676328569b5bb4acd4e792fd6c7af932391b625915f768e9cf989243045eaf29"} {"question" "q-3762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-3762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "-\\infty "] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\infty "] ["text" "Does not exist."]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-3762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-339426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{3-x-8{x}^{2}}{k\\,{x}^{2}+7x-4}=\\frac{2}{5},$  what is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-339426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{3-x-8{x}^{2}}{k\\,{x}^{2}+7x-4} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{8{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{k{x}^{2}}{\\,{x}^{2}}+\\frac{7x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{x}-8)}{(k+\\frac{7}{x}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-0-8}{k+0-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8}{k} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{8}{k} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 2k & =-40 \\\\ k & =-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-339426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "676328569b5bb4acd4e792fd6c7af932391b625915f768e9cf989243045eaf29"} {"question" "q-339426" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-339426" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-20"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-48842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{|6x-2|}{8x+5}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-48842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For large positive values of $x,$ we have $|6x-2|=6x-2.$ Consequently, for $x\\to \\infty ,$ we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{|6x-2|}{8x+5}={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{6x-2}{8x+5}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{1}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{6x-2}{8x+5} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{6x}{x}-\\frac{2}{x})}{(\\frac{8x}{x}+\\frac{5}{x})} \\\\  & {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(6-\\frac{2}{x})}{(8+\\frac{5}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-0}{8-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-48842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "676328569b5bb4acd4e792fd6c7af932391b625915f768e9cf989243045eaf29"} {"question" "q-48842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-48842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-48842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-48878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{|10x+3|}{6-5x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-48878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For large positive values of $x,$ we have $|10x+3|=10x+3.$ Consequently, for $x\\to \\infty ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{|10x+3|}{6-5x}=\\frac{10x+3}{6-5x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{1}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{10x+3}{6-5x} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{10x}{x}+\\frac{3}{x})}{(\\frac{6}{x}-\\frac{5x}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(10+\\frac{3}{x})}{(\\frac{6}{x}-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+0}{0-5} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-48878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "676328569b5bb4acd4e792fd6c7af932391b625915f768e9cf989243045eaf29"} {"question" "q-48878" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-48878" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-48878" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-68048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{4{x}^{5}-9}{{x}^{3}+8x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-68048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{4{x}^{5}-9}{{x}^{3}+8x} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{4{x}^{5}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{9}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{8x}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(4{x}^{2}-\\frac{9}{{x}^{3}})}{(1+\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{4{x}^{2}-0}{1+0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }4{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-68048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "676328569b5bb4acd4e792fd6c7af932391b625915f768e9cf989243045eaf29"} {"question" "q-68048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-68048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\infty "] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1/4"] ["math" "\\infty "] ["text" "Does not exist."]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-68048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\infty "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-3761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{{x}^{4}-6}{{x}^{2}-x+2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-3761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{{x}^{4}-6}{{x}^{2}-x+2} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{({x}^{2}-\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}})}{(1-\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{({x}^{2}-0)}{(1-0+0)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061351/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ddf5288019cfd5f3c4cb4ed49b8844a48d3681d6b3bf5237b26060e29f8e3c6"} {"question" "q-37